'''Million-Dollar Cat''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Download Celebration! (Event Gacha)|Download Celebration!]] Event Gacha. It was added in [[Version 11.0 Update|Version 11.0]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 635
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Million-Dollar Cat
|name2 = Hundred-Million-Dollar Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Hundred-Million-Dollar Cat''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Million-Dollar Cat is a fairly situational unit. It has a 100% chance to perform [[Critical Hit]]s at 350 range, with no drawn out foreswing animation like units such as [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] or [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Corrupted Moneko]]. However, it has a 16 second attack rate, mirroring the long attack rate seen with [[Sunny Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Sunny Neneko]]. In that respect, Million-Dollar Cat performs best when handling enemies in low quantities. Its abysmal damage also prevents its usage against the upper echelon of Metal enemies with 1k+ HP, such as [[Super Metal Hippoe]] or [[Sir Metal Seal]]. This doesn't mean its entirely useless though; it can easily pick off higher ranged threats in [[Pure Gold R.Ost]]/[[Koronium]] (so long as the latter doesn't get a chance to unleash a [[Wave Attack]]). While one might assume you can use it to take care of [[CyberFace]], Million-Dollar Cat's damage is so low that it needs to be at least level '''46''' to kill it.

Additionally, its [[Money Up]] ability provides an incentive to use Million-Dollar Cat over other Critical Hitters when facing off against [[Metal Hippoe]], [[Metal Doge]], or any of the aforementioned low HP Metal threats. Considering how many Metal stages tend to be stringent with cash, it finds excellent usage in stages with even just a few annoying Metal peons.

